Files from other packages

This package bundles no code or data from the packages below, so their licence texts are not
repeated here. @inkbar/core depends on them, and they reach a host's build in these ways:

- The engine's binary and worker (inkbar-pdfium.wasm and worker.mjs), from @inkbar/engine, which
  the Vite plugin copies into the build. The binary is PDFium and the libraries linked into it,
  each under its own licence; dist/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES in @inkbar/engine carries all of them,
  and the plugin copies it beside the two files as THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.
- The fallback fonts (Noto Sans and Noto Sans CJK), from @inkbar/fonts, which the Vite plugin
  copies into the build. They are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, with the copyright notices
  in OFL.txt in @inkbar/fonts, which the plugin copies beside the fonts as fonts/OFL.txt.
- The form script sandbox: pdf.sandbox.mjs, which a bundler takes from pdfjs-dist when core
  imports it, and quickjs-eval.js and quickjs-eval.wasm, which the Vite plugin copies from
  pdfjs-dist/wasm/ into the build. pdfjs-dist is under the Apache License 2.0, in its LICENSE,
  and ships no other licence for the two files; the plugin copies that LICENSE beside them as
  sandbox/LICENSE.

A host that copies these files by hand, or ships them on, keeps those licences with them.
